 stretch to say that this is  because ganondorf has been here at the  brink of death but not quite dead the  whole time this also implies that so  long as one male gerudo is alive in this  case ganondorf another cannot be born  that's all well and good but right about  now you're probably wondering what the  point of this video is and i'm so glad  you asked see i pointed out the gerudo  male pattern birth rate in order to  scrutinize something that people rarely  ever talk about and that is the  existence of male gerudo kings before  ganondorf by the time ganondorf was born  prior to the events of ocarina of time  there had already been the legend set in  gerudo law that once every hundred years  a male would be born to the otherwise  all-female tribe and that said male must  be crowned king obviously since this was  already gerudo law according to naburu  it must mean that there were an  unknowable number of gerudo men that  existed and ruled the gerudo as kings  before ganondorf right but with there  being no mention of the gerudo before  ocarina of time in the timeline is it  possible to know anything about these  mysterious other gerudo kings well  obviously this is going to be mostly  speculative but i'd like to propose a  possibility for the identities of the  previous gerudo men that would also  serve to explain the absence of any  other gerudomans since ganondorf's reign  in the distant past see the legend of  zelda is a balanced one the symbol of  the series the triforce exists as a  perfect three-way balance of three even  sides its wielders zelda link and  ganondorf are extensions of this balance  and are each chosen by the goddesses  regardless of whether or not they  possess pieces of the triforce currently  logically they must then also be  balanced with one another and share some  similarities in order to maintain this  symbolism but with one of them being  over seven feet tall another being a  princess and the last one being peter  pan you might be wondering what exactly  is supposed to be similar about them  well instead of looking at physical  characteristics let's back up and  instead look at the meta-narrative link  is not the only link right he's the  incarnation or reincarnation of the  spirit of the hero which manifests each  time as a pretty similar looking  individual all things considered you  know as a young man or even child that's  normally blonde haired and normally  blue-eyed zelda also reincarnates but  even more directly since every single  daughter born into the royal family is  named zelda and is a direct descendant  of the original zelda who was actually  the straight-up incarnation of goddess  hylia i'd like to propose that in  balance with the other two chosen  reincarnating individuals ganondorf also  reincarnates and here are two pieces of  evidence to support my gannon notion  get it anyway the first one is perhaps a  bit debatable since some fans actually  don't take four swords adventures as  canon but in that game which takes place  following the events of twilight  princess and therefore the death of  ganondorf in the child timeline there  actually was another male gerudo born  and his name was ganondorf who went on  to you know turn into ganon and try to  dominate the world and stuff this of  course supports the notion that he  reincarnated for that game the second  proof is a bit of cut text from the game  twilight princess which i actually  featured in my obscure ganondorf facts  video which i'll link in the description  below if you'd like to check out the cut  text happens at the end of the game when  ganondorf has been fatally wounded by  link and the master sword originally  ganondorf was supposed to say quote when  the chosen ones appear they are always  born into this world in perfect balance  when this world brings forth another  marked as you are know too that it shall  also be visited by one of my blood if  this doesn't scream reincarnation i  don't know what does what's even more  interesting is that he implies with the  cut text that he will not only  reincarnate like link but that when he  does it will be as a descendant of his  own bloodline like zelda and since his  own bloodline would be the bloodline of  the gerudo that means that his  descendant would therefore be another  gerudo right another gerudo man once  every hundred years see now it's all  coming together so all we have to do to  figure this puzzle out is not only apply  it to the gerudo going forward in the  timeline but also going backwards just  like we can with the royal family since  zelda's reincarnating bloodline traces  its origin all the way back to the  goddess hylia one could then assume that  ganondorf's reincarnating bloodline  traces its origin all the way back to  the demon demise this would mean that  just like the hylian princesses before  zelda were all zeldas the gerudo kings  before ganondorf were all ganondorfs the  question that remains though is that if  there really were an unknowable number  of ganondorfs that existed before  ocarina of time then why haven't we  heard about them or read about them in  the ages on the timeline i think in this  case the simplest answer is probably the  correct one and what i mean by that is  that just like not all incarnations of  zelda have to rise to the occasion to  save the world perhaps not all  incarnations of ganondorf have to rise  to the occasion to end it who knows some  of them may have actually ruled  benevolently and before i wrap up this  theory here's a little bonus speculation  since i'm sure this is on some of your  minds it is true that this is all due to  the curse that demise placed on the  bloodline of the goddess hylia and it's  also true that his hatred has not only  incarnated as ganondorf it's also  appeared as other demons across the  series but that could actually have an  explanation as well if you've seen my  recent theory on demise's master sword  you probably already know where i'm  going with this but just in case you  missed it i'll link to it in the  description below if you want to check  it out in further detail in a nutshell  though it could be that gear rahim also  known as demise's master sword or rather  his living weapon is responsible for the  creation of these demons such as vati or  maladus or ganon and subsequently even  malice while his weapon is creating the  demons his physical incarnation in  perfect balance with hylia has  manifested as the reincarnating mortal  known as ganondorf what do you think huh  did we speculate and figure out who the  gerudo kings before ganondorf were or is  it you know still completely unknowable  until we potentially get a game before  ocarina of time let me know in the  comments below also thank you so much  for watching if you enjoyed the video  please consider leaving a like as it  really helps with getting it spread  around on youtube and into the  recommended pages of zelda fans just  like you and me and make sure you're  subscribed if you haven't done so  already so that you're right here for  all the super sweet nintendo stuff to  come huge thanks as always to my amazing  bandit crew of which i have a new name  to announce please say hello to ivan  knight who has recently joined the ranks  of my elite if you watching are in a  comfortable position and interested in  helping these videos get made and  supporting an internet weirdo like  myself please feel free to check out  that join button located below or follow  the links in the description for my  patreon and merch pages that's all i've  got for this one so as always i hope you  have a wonderful rest of your day this  is mass nintendo bandit looking forward  to seeing you on down the trail and  signing out  [Music]

